request.description:
An array of records, each thirteen native-endian 32-bit integers.
Lengths and positions are 24.8 fixed point, in surface-local
logical pixels:

x, y, width, height and radius: a rounded rectangle, a control;
kind: 0 a well, cut into the glass, 1 a bead, standing out of it;
depth: how deep the well, or how high the bead, at rest;
press: 0 to 255, how far it's pressed in: a well deepens, most
around the light;
milk: 0 to 255, how milky the glass turns inside it, up to fill_x:
where it's on. There the client's drawn accent (white) is the milky
glass, and the rest of what it drew there stays as drawn, dark ink
on it;
fill_x: where the milk ends, across; past the right edge for all
of it;
light_x, light_y: where the finger is;
light: 0 to 255, how bright a soft light around it is.

A relief changes the glass of the island it's in only: outside
every glass record it's ignored. New requests go last, here: a
request's number is its place in the interface. The initial value is empty. At
most 64 records: the compositor ignores the rest, and 64 keeps the
request inside one Wayland message (4096 bytes).
